  "question": {
    "text": "A longitudinal wave is represented by $x=x_0 \\sin 2 \\pi(n t-x / \\lambda)$. The maximum particle velocity will be four times the wave velocity if:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bxQhZ",
      "text": "$\\lambda=\\frac{\\pi x_0}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "T4xBE",
      "text": "$\\lambda=2 \\pi x_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8fxuu",
      "text": "$\\lambda=\\frac{\\pi x_0}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NtYQV",
      "text": "$\\lambda=4 \\pi x_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: Maximum particle velocity $\\left(\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{p}}\\right)=\\mathrm{A} \\omega=2 \\pi n x_0$\nWave velocity $\\left(\\mathrm{V}_\\omega\\right)=n \\lambda$\nHere, $\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{P}}=4 \\mathrm{~V}_\\omega$\n$$\n2 \\pi n x_0=4 n \\lambda\n$$\n$$\n\\lambda=\\frac{\\pi}{2} x_0\n$$",
